Human: How can I get a cheaper car insurance rate?

Assistant: There are a lot of ways to get a cheaper car insurance rate, including:

Reducing your insurance deductibles (the amount you have to pay out of pocket before your coverage kicks in);

Reducing your insurance coverage (i.e. the extent of your coverage, i.e. what types of claims your insurance company will pay out for, such as liability or comprehensive);

Increasing your deductibles in order to lower the amount you pay out of pocket for claims. For example, if your car insurance costs $50 every six months, reducing it to $25 every six months will save you $25.

Increasing your coverage can be expensive, and it is usually not recommended unless your coverage exceeds $100,000 or so.
